---
title: Hex shift
tags: tools
heading: "Shift hex"
summary: >-
    Shifts every byte of hex up or down by a set amount, so <code class="tool-example">48 65 6c 6c 6f</code> [Hello] shifted by 1 becomes <code class="tool-example">49 66 6d 6d 70</code> [Ifmmp].
---
{% from "macros/tool.njk" import toolSection with context %}
{% from "macros/tool-frame.njk" import toolFrame %}
{% from "macros/delimiter.njk" import delimiter %}
{% set filename = page.fileSlug %}
{% set intro %}
    <p>A lazy shift: every byte moves up or down by the same amount. Positive numbers shift to the right, as in the +1 above, and negative numbers are allowed and shift to the left: shifted by -1, it becomes <code class="tool-example">47 64 6b 6b 6e</code> [Gdkkn].</p>
    <p>Your hex can use any of the usual delimiters between bytes (spaces, hyphens, colons, commas, semicolons, new lines, \x, 0x or %), or none, and they can be mixed. The delimiter dropdown chooses how the result is written.</p>
{% endset %}
{% call toolSection(intro) %}
{% call toolFrame(filename, "Shift hex", placeholder = "Example: 48 65 6c 6c 6f", tabs = ["Text", "Hex", "Binary", "Base64", "Decimal"], actions = [{ id: filename + "Run", label: "Shift" }]) %}
<div class="tool-field tool-field--short">
    <label class="tool-field__label" for="{{ filename }}Value">Shift<span class="visually-hidden"> each byte by</span></label>
    <input type="number" class="form-control" id="{{ filename }}Value" autocomplete="off" value="1" aria-describedby="{{ filename }}Status">
</div>
<div class="tool-field">
    <label class="tool-field__label" for="{{ filename }}Delimiter"><span class="visually-hidden">Hex </span>Delimiter</label>
    {{ delimiter(filename) }}
</div>
{% endcall %}
{% endcall %}
